    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This study investigates the alignment and implementation of inclusive education policies within Egypt relative to global standards. Grounded in world society theory, the research explores the extent to which Egypt’s educational policies converge with international norms or diverge due to implementation challenges. Through qualitative document analysis, the study examines Egypt’s national policies such as the 2014 Constitution (amended in 2019), Law No. 10 (2018), and the Education 2.0 reform plan (2018). Findings highlight significant legislative advancements in Egypt yet reveal gaps in practical implementation. The research underscores the necessity of bridging policy and practice to enhance Egypt’s educational inclusivity. The analysis contributes to the broader understanding of inclusion, offering insights for policy refinement to promote a more inclusive and equitable education system within Egypt.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Youssef, D. (2024). A Comparative Analysis of Inclusive Education Policies: Global Norms and Egypt’s Journey Toward Access and Equity. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/ff578jt1203. https://doi.org/10.25740/ff578jt1203.",
            "type": "preferred citation",
